# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/octo-t8 four-card DEVELOPMENT window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/octo-t8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled in by whoever drives the window (@K64J_GRAFT_DIR@ and @K64J_TTNNCPP_SHA256@: the K64j graft directory and its binary's
# digest); every other value is final. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo-1 is the placeholder every template carries (sed -i 's/tp4-octo-1/<tag>/' *.env); these one-card jobs run the harness in its own pinned image
# and mount this checkout's scripts as the code under test, so they do not need B0's image. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# AN EVIDENCE JOB, ONE CARD: the cardm action (C2_CARDS=pair: cardm is a pair-shaped step) runs one harness on card M alone; the quad jobs reset all four boards, this one never does.
# NO NEW GRAFT: octo-T8 changes no K64j kernel and no factory. 0x21 (tail | extent) is an existing K64j flag set - CB1 qualified it at G8B2 and G4B3, one KV head - and the octo block's
# bundle of ONE eight-row group (G8B1) is that program at B = 1. The graft is the SERVED one: the same _ttnncpp.so the C2 image carries (docker/qwen-c2-serving.Dockerfile), pinned by
# EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256 - read the launched argv, a graft mounted is not a graft executed. What no card has run is the bundle of one eight-row group; that is what Q1 qualifies.
# Q2 (EVIDENCE): the same at full scope: UB - ONE batched launch of eight users == eight per-user launches, every output and prefix-state byte and the untouched initial states, bit for bit, and
# the HEAD-SLICE equivalence against the PINNED pair launch (24 heads, the qualified program) fed the same twelve heads - and NT, the single-user native twin under the four-card view == the batched launch,
# per user; seeds 17, 18, 19; with the launches timed (the 96-core wave against eight per-user launches). READ: 'GDN_TP4 verdict=PASS scope=octo ... differing=0 ... geometry=8x8' and the timing rows.
# Duration (estimate): 5-10 min. Stop rule: a FAIL stops the window (no fallback to two launches of four is built: that would be a new piece, decided by the owner).
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/k64j/run_card_b.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--sections UB,NT --users 8 --rows 8 --seeds 17,18,19 --iterations 20
C2_CARDM_ENV=K64J_HARNESS=gdn_tp4 TP4_WIDTH=4 KOPGRAFT64=@K64J_GRAFT_DIR@ EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256=@K64J_TTNNCPP_SHA256@
